TITLE:: MapperWindow
summary:: the mapper's window: controllers, targets, learn, every mapping
categories:: Libraries>Mapper
related:: Classes/Mapper, Classes/MapperMap

DESCRIPTION::
code::
Mapper.default.gui;
Mapper.default.gui.select([\tidal, \cut]);
::

On the left, everything that can be mapped now, as a tree: a provider (a mixer, a module, a
set of effects), its groups, the targets in each. A provider starts open, a group folded; click
a heading to open or fold it, strong::+:: and strong::-:: do them all. The menu and the field
narrow the tree, and typing opens everything that matches. A dot marks the mapped targets, and
a heading counts them. Pointing at a row says in the hint bar what it is - a target's kind, its
range, where it is now, its address and what is mapped to it; a provider may add a line of its
own (a code::hint:: in the description it gives, see link::Classes/MapperTarget::). Pick a
target and it is on show on the right; a target selected from elsewhere is brought into view.
The strong::targets:: button folds the whole panel away - it is only needed to pick a target
by name.

On the right, the controllers: strong::find:: lists the devices plugged in, strong::connect::
listens to one under a name, strong::forget:: lets it go with its mappings. Then the mappings,
by controller and element, so the targets of one control sit together - the second and later
ones start with a plus. Under the list, the one on show: lo and hi in the target's own units,
invert, takeover, the button mode and the curve, which is drawn by dragging its points.

strong::midi learn:: switches the mapper's learn mode: click a fader, a knob or a switch in any
window that follows it, move a control, and again until it is off. strong::learn:: maps the next
element moved to the target on show; a control that already moves something keeps that as well.
strong::+ tidal:: learns a Tidal control by name, strong::code...:: opens every mapping as code.

The window keeps nothing: closing it changes no mapping.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: mapper
a link::Classes/Mapper::. link::Classes/Mapper#-gui:: is the usual way in.

METHOD:: windowBounds
Where it opens; remembered when it closes.

METHOD:: showTargets
Whether the panel of targets is on show. The window sets it; set it before opening one to
start folded.

METHOD:: treeOpen
Which headings of the tree are open, by their path ("AdaptiveTextures/tex/loop"). Kept between
windows.

METHOD:: treeRowHeight
METHOD:: panelWidth
The height of a row of the tree and the width of its panel, in points.

METHOD:: shortLabel
A target's label without the words the headings above it already say.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: treeRows
The rows of the tree on show, top to bottom: Events with code::kind:: (code::\folder:: or
code::\leaf::), code::label::, code::depth::, and for a target its code::address::.

METHOD:: select
Put a target on show, with its mapping if it has one. From any thread.

METHOD:: selectedAddress

METHOD:: selectedMap

METHOD:: follow
Whether a mapping moved on the controller comes on show.

METHOD:: refresh

METHOD:: find
Look for controllers.

METHOD:: openCode
Every mapping as a document.

METHOD:: isOpen

METHOD:: front

METHOD:: close
